WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.340
Bill C-14 received Royal Assent on June 17th, 2016.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.079
RCMP Commissioner Bob Paulson held command.

00:00:08.079 --> 00:00:13.034
Bill C-7 received Royal Assent on March 17th, 2021.

00:00:13.034 --> 00:00:15.784
Commissioner Brenda Lucki held command.

00:00:15.784 --> 00:00:21.874
Seventy-six thousand seven hundred and seven total MAID deaths between 2016 and 2024.

00:00:21.875 --> 00:00:28.613
The reasonably foreseeable death clause was removed — expanding eligibility to chronic illness and eventually mental health.

00:00:28.613 --> 00:00:34.386
Zero RCMP interventions against the legislation despite documented Rome Statute applicability.

00:00:34.386 --> 00:00:38.181
Nuremberg Code violations documented in the expansion process.

00:00:38.181 --> 00:00:41.420
Canada's last execution was in 1962.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:44.977
Capital punishment was abolished in 1976.

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:48.909
Medical assistance in dying was legalized in 2016.

00:00:48.909 --> 00:00:50.727
The state did not stop killing.

00:00:50.727 --> 00:00:52.420
It rebranded the process.
